#### Principle 2: Tailwind CSS Owns All Visual Output

**Description:** All colours, spacing, typography, border radius, shadows, and responsive breakpoints are expressed as Tailwind CSS utility classes or CSS custom properties consumed by Tailwind. No inline styles. No external CSS-in-JS libraries (Emotion, styled-components).

**Rationale:** Tailwind CSS utilities colocate styles with components, are tree-shakeable at build time (unused utilities purged), and integrate directly with Shadcn/UI's component model. CSS-in-JS libraries like Emotion (used by Material UI) add runtime overhead and cannot be mixed cleanly with Tailwind without specificity conflicts.

**Design Token System:**

```css
/* globals.css — all design tokens as CSS custom properties */
:root {
  --background: 0 0% 100%;
  --foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;
  --primary: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;
  --primary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;
  --muted: 210 40% 96.1%;
  --muted-foreground: 215.4 16.3% 46.9%;
  --border: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;
  --radius: 0.5rem;
  /* State-specific overrides applied at :root or [data-tenant="state-tx"] */
}
```

Tailwind CSS maps these tokens via `tailwind.config.ts`:

```typescript
theme: {
  extend: {
    colors: {
      background: 'hsl(var(--background))',
      foreground: 'hsl(var(--foreground))',
      primary: {
        DEFAULT: 'hsl(var(--primary))',
        foreground: 'hsl(var(--primary-foreground))',
      },
      border: 'hsl(var(--border))',
    },
    borderRadius: {
      lg: 'var(--radius)',
      md: 'calc(var(--radius) - 2px)',
      sm: 'calc(var(--radius) - 4px)',
    },
  },
}
```

Per-state theming: swap the CSS custom property values at the tenant root element. No component changes required.

**Application:** Every new component uses only Tailwind utility classes for styling. CSS Modules are used only for component-specific styles that Tailwind cannot express (e.g., complex animations, pseudo-element content). Inline `style={{}}` is prohibited except for dynamic computed values (e.g., chart dimensions, virtualised row positions).

